# Delegation & Role Rules (Mestre)

## The Mestre does NOT
- Run `./validate.sh`, `npm test`, `jest`, `npm run test:e2e`, or any test command.
- Run lint/tsc/build as a substitute for the QA Tester.
- Weaken, modify, or delete tests to make them pass.
- Implement a change without `.specs/changes/<name>/.approved` present (ask the user first).
- Execute tests during the RPI/spec phase (writing proposal/design/tasks/specs).

## All validation is delegated
- Any test execution (unit, e2e, validate, build checks) MUST be delegated to the **QA Tester** agent via `maestri ask "Tester" ...`.
- The Mestre only writes code/specs and delegates validation; the QA Tester reports results.
- When reporting, the QA Tester must not weaken assertions — fix implementation or escalate to the user.

## QA Tester capabilities
- The QA Tester MAY use the attached browser (portal) to perform end-to-end/UI tests when needed (e.g., smoke tests, visual checks, form flows).
- Browser-based validation is allowed and encouraged for frontend changes when it adds coverage beyond unit/e2e tests.

## Spec approval gate
- Before implementing, verify `.specs/changes/<name>/.approved` exists.
- If missing, stop and ask the user; do not implement.
- Helper: `./check-approval.sh <change-name>`. Create the marker only after explicit user approval.

## Test plan is mandatory
- Every change under `.specs/changes/<name>/` MUST define tests in `tasks.md` with exact file path, test case, and assertion.
- No "add tests later". Unit → `src/**/*.spec.ts`; E2E → `test/**/*.e2e-spec.ts` (supertest); infra → assert real behavior (e.g., `listIndexes()`).